{"id":"dbxtool.1","n":"dbxtool","s":"1","src":{"r":{"pkg":"fwupd","ver":"1.9.26-1.el9.rocky.0.1","repo":"BaseOS","url":"https://dl.rockylinux.org/vault/rocky/9.6/BaseOS/x86_64/os/Packages/f/fwupd-1.9.26-1.el9.rocky.0.1.x86_64.rpm","path":"/usr/share/man/man1/dbxtool.1.gz","sha256":"3b417c4fda9d4f0ed934f0228f774af14b6fec81d7da1af636a2a0761d8e22f3","date":"","origin":"1.9.26"},"u":{"pkg":"fwupd","ver":"2.0.20-1ubuntu2~22.04.2","repo":"jammy-updates/main","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/f/fwupd/fwupd_2.0.20-1ubuntu2~22.04.2_amd64.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man1/dbxtool.1.gz","sha256":"ccf2d533e302072f30bea1f26fa9f80c017585ee93bd5e04af5d0375b2d5d188","date":"","origin":"2.0.20"}},"nopt":{"r":0,"u":0},"desc":"modify the dbx revocation list","same":false,"r":[["NAME","<p><b>dbxtool</b> — modify the dbx revocation list</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p><b>dbxtool</b> [CMD]</p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p>This manual page documents briefly the <b>dbxtool</b> command.</p> <p><b>dbxtool</b> allows a user to operate on the UEFI dbx revocation list. This tool can be used to list the current dbx contents or update it to a newer version.</p>"],["OPTIONS","<p>The dbxtool command takes various options depending on the action. Run <b>dbxtool --help</b> for the full list.</p>"],["BUGS","<p>See GitHub Issues: &lt;https://github.com/fwupd/fwupd/issues&gt;</p>"],["SEE ALSO","<p>&lt;fwupdtool(1)&gt; &lt;fwupdmgr(1)&gt;</p>"]],"u":[["NAME","<p><b>dbxtool</b> - modify the dbx revocation list</p>"],["SYNOPSIS",1],["DESCRIPTION",2],["OPTIONS",3],["BUGS",4],["SEE ALSO",5]],"diff":{"r":[],"u":[]}}